# Runtime view

{% callout type="info" title="About this chapter" %}
Use a few important scenarios to show how the building blocks interact at runtime – for example core workflows, failure cases or system startup.
{% /callout %}

## Completing a delivery (offline)

{% steps %}
{% step title="Load the route" %}
Before setting off, the app downloads the route from the app backend and stores it locally.
{% /step %}
{% step title="Record the delivery" %}
The driver confirms the delivery with a signature and a photo – even without mobile reception.
{% /step %}
{% step title="Synchronize" %}
As soon as a connection is available, the app sends all updates in the correct order. The app backend publishes the `DeliveryCompleted` event.
{% /step %}
{% step title="Update the live view" %}
The live view processes the event and refreshes the dispatch screen within two seconds.
{% /step %}
{% /steps %}

{% details title="Failure case: duplicate messages" %}
Every message carries a unique ID. The app backend discards duplicates, so repeated transmissions are harmless (idempotent processing).
{% /details %}
